# When fixing an issue (e.g. from Github issues) please:

1. find where is the right place to add a new unit test to reproduce the issue
2. add a new unit test
3. run tests to see if the test really fails (`nix develop -c python -m pytest` or the focused file)
4. fix the issue until tests pass
5. clean up — run **post-change-refactor** on the uncommitted change
6. run the full suite at last to confirm things are still working

If a fix / make-test-pass attempt overruns the time-box (~5 min scrutinize, >10 min hard stop): stop, revert or stash WIP, and use **slice-plan-refinement** on the current PLAN (`.cursor/rules/problem-decomposition.mdc`). If there is no PLAN yet, use **slice-planning** first.

